Retry a main-frame load that fails, and validate launch loads

Every load of the launch argument, the first and each reload 0002 or this
patch makes, carries Cache-Control: no-cache, so it is validated with its
server: with the server down it fails rather than showing a cached copy.
When the main frame's load fails, for any reason WebKit shows its error
page for, load the launch argument again 5 s later, and again after
every failure until a load succeeds. WebKit's error page stays up
meanwhile. A browser that starts before its backend listens, or whose
reload lands during a backend restart, is no longer left on the error page
or on a cached page that cannot reach its backend.

This is C inside surf's load handling, so it cannot be a bbappend change.

Applies after 0002-reload-a-page-that-stops-answering.patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [kiosk-specific]
